// ─── Notifications (Section 6.1) ─────────────────────────────────────────────

enum NotificationKind {
  REPLY
  HELP_OFFER
  GROUP
  CONNECTION
  REVIEW
  VERIFICATION
  ANNOUNCEMENT
  // Feed reactions. Their own kinds so the client can give them their own icon rather than
  // falling back to a grey announcement row.
  LIKE
  BOOKMARK
  // Bookings and shop orders, which share the `BOOKINGS` preference row. One kind rather than two:
  // the icon is the same and the route already says which of the two it is.
  BOOKING
  /// A step somebody ticked on a deal. Shares the BOOKINGS row: it is the same kind of business.
  DEAL
  /// A warning, a removal, a suspension — anything staff did that the member has to be told about.
  ///
  /// Its own kind because it cannot be muted: it sits in the locked `ACCOUNT` preference category,
  /// so a member who has turned every notification off still hears that their post was removed and
  /// how to appeal. A notification somebody can switch off is not a notice (§7.3).
  MODERATION
}

/**
 * Computed server-side in the member's timezone (D32). Deriving it on the device
 * means the grouping shifts as a phone crosses midnight or changes country, and
 * two devices on one account disagree.
 */
/// Diagnosis only. Push routes by token, so a wrong or missing platform costs nothing.
